by fritzmg at 2026-01-07T12:30:00Z

> this would be rejected. Those headers to bypass are an implementation detail, related to the way the API used by the bridge works. It does not make sense to make that configurable from the outside. If something is missing in the bridge, the solution is to fix the issue in the bridge, not to introduce a public extension point.

The reason this comes up at all is because other bundles might add their own headers to a message - and they might not use the `X-` prefix. The [prefix has been deprecated](https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc6648) for a while now - but Symfony itself still uses it, e.g. `X-Transport` and `X-Bus-Transport`. Technically these should be changed as well - but then the same problem would arise with the Graph Mailer there.

Ideally Microsoft should change this on their end and simply ignore any headers they do not know/support.

